From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skytech <iot.dmitech@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mt8365-evk: drop HDMI dai-link from sound card

The Skytech Genio 350 board has no IT66121 HDMI bridge responding on
I2C (1-004c), so the IT66121 driver never binds and the hdmi-codec DAI
is never registered. Because the sound card's I2S_OUT_BE link points
at &it66121_hdmi, parse_dai_link_info() returns -EPROBE_DEFER forever
and no ALSA card is created ("No soundcards found").

Remove the HDMI dai-link so the card registers with the internal
MT6357 codec (MTK_Codec link). I2S_OUT_BE falls back to the dummy
codec, so PCM device numbering (and asound.conf) is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8365-evk.dts | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8365-evk.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8365-evk.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8365-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8365-evk.dts
@@ -158,15 +158,6 @@
 		pinctrl-4 = <&aud_mosi_off_pins>;
 		pinctrl-5 = <&aud_mosi_on_pins>;
 		mediatek,platform = <&afe>;
-
-		/* hdmi interface */
-		dai-link-0 {
-			link-name = "I2S_OUT_BE";
-			sound-dai = <&afe>;
-			codec {
-				sound-dai = <&it66121_hdmi>;
-			};
-		};
 	};
 
 	vsys_lcm_reg: regulator-vsys-lcm {
-- 
2.43.0
